## Prerequisites

- Python [[.PythonVersion]] or newer
[[- if .UV]]
- [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) for dependency management
[[- end]]
[[- if .Docker]]
- Docker, for the [[.DatabaseLabel]] container
[[- end]]
[[- if .Tailwind]]
- Node.js and [[.Node]], to build the Tailwind stylesheet
[[- end]]

## Setup

```bash
[[- if .UV]]
uv sync
[[- else]]
python -m venv .venv
.venv/bin/python -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
[[- end]]
[ -f .env ] || cp .env.example .env
[[- if .Tailwind]]
[[.Node]] install
[[.Node]] run build:css
[[- end]]
[[- if .Docker]]
docker compose up -d --wait db
[[- end]]
[[.Python]] manage.py migrate
[[.Python]] manage.py createsuperuser
[[.Python]] manage.py runserver
```

No superuser is created for you. Run `createsuperuser` above, then sign in at
`/[[.AdminURL]]`.
[[- if not .UV]] On Windows the interpreter is `.venv\Scripts\python.exe`.[[end]]

`.env.example` ships a placeholder `SECRET_KEY` so the project boots immediately.
Replace it before you deploy anything:

```bash
[[.Python]] -c 'import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(50))'
```

[[if .Tailwind]]## Styles

Tailwind compiles `assets/tailwind.css` into `static/dist/styles.css`, scanning the
templates and the Python files that carry classes. Keep it rebuilding while you work:

```bash
[[.Node]] run watch:css
```

The compiled stylesheet is committed, so a deploy needs no Node. Run
`[[.Node]] run build:css` and commit the result whenever templates change.

[[end]]## Environment

`ENVIRONMENT` is the only switch for `DEBUG`. Set it to `local`, `test`, `staging`
or `production`; `DEBUG` is on for `local` and `test`. Everything that behaves differently in development — the browsable
API, plain-text logging, the browser-reload endpoint — reads that one value.

[[if .Pydantic -]]
Configuration is validated at startup by `[[.ModuleName]]/conf.py`.
A missing or malformed variable stops the process with a message naming the field
rather than failing later at the point of use.
[[- else -]]
Configuration is read at startup. A missing variable, or a value that does not
parse — a boolean other than true/false, on/off, yes/no or 1/0, or a number
that is not one — stops the process rather than failing later at the point of use.
[[- end]]

## Configuration

`.env.example` lists what every environment needs. The variables below are
optional; set them in `.env` or in the process environment when you need them.

Email, read in staging and production:

| Variable | Example |
|----------|---------|
| `EMAIL_HOST` | `smtp.gmail.com` |
| `EMAIL_PORT` | `587` |
| `EMAIL_USE_TLS` | `True` |
| `EMAIL_HOST_USER` | |
| `EMAIL_HOST_PASSWORD` | |
| `DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL` | `no-reply@yourdomain.com`[[if .AccountEmail]]; production refuses Django's `webmaster@localhost`[[end]] |

Production security, read in staging and production:

| Variable | Example |
|----------|---------|
| `ADMIN_URL` | `admin/` |
| `CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS` | `https://example.com` |
| `SECURE_SSL_REDIRECT` | `True` |
| `SECURE_HSTS_SECONDS` | `31536000` |
| `SECURE_HSTS_INCLUDE_SUBDOMAINS` | `False` |
| `SECURE_HSTS_PRELOAD` | `False` |
| `TRUST_PROXY_SSL_HEADER` | `False` |
[[- if .Sentry]]

Error tracking with Sentry, off until `SENTRY_DSN` is set:

| Variable | Example |
|----------|---------|
| `SENTRY_DSN` | the DSN of your Sentry project |
| `SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT` | defaults to `ENVIRONMENT`; set it only to report under another name |
| `SENTRY_RELEASE` | |
| `SENTRY_SEND_PII` | `False` |
| `SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE` | `0.1` |
| `SENTRY_PROFILE_SESSION_SAMPLE_RATE` | `0.1` |
[[- end]]

