## Deployment

```bash
[[if .MultiEnv]]export DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE=[[.ModuleName]].settings.production
[[end]][[if .UV]]uv sync --no-dev --frozen[[else]].venv/bin/python -m pip install -r requirements.txt[[end]]
[[.DeployPython]] manage.py migrate --noinput
[[.DeployPython]] manage.py createcachetable
[[.DeployPython]] manage.py collectstatic --noinput
[[.DeployPython]] manage.py check --deploy
[[.DeployTool]] gunicorn [[.ModuleName]].wsgi:application --bind 0.0.0.0:8000
```

Static files are served by WhiteNoise, so no separate web server is required for
them. `check --deploy` warns that HSTS covers neither subdomains nor the preload
list: set `SECURE_HSTS_INCLUDE_SUBDOMAINS` and `SECURE_HSTS_PRELOAD` to `True` once
every subdomain serves HTTPS, because leaving the preload list takes months. Set
`TRUST_PROXY_SSL_HEADER=True` only behind a proxy that overwrites
`X-Forwarded-Proto`.[[if .AccountEmail]] Set `DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL` to an address your mail server
sends from: production refuses Django's default, `webmaster@localhost`.[[end]]
[[- if .MultiEnv]] Copy `.env.production.example` to `.env` on the server and fill it in.

`manage.py` defaults to `settings.local` and gunicorn to `settings.production`. Export
`DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE` before running management commands on a server: it is read before
`.env`, so it has no effect there. `settings.local` refuses to start unless `ENVIRONMENT=local`,
and `settings.production` refuses to start with it.
[[- else]] On the server, set `ENVIRONMENT=production` and the variables from `.env.example` in
the process environment or in `.env`.
[[- end]]

## Layout

| Path | What lives there |
|------|------------------|
| `[[.ModuleName]]/` | settings, URLs, WSGI/ASGI and the health check[[if not .Templates]] and JSON error handlers[[end]] |
[[- if .MultiEnv]]
| `[[.ModuleName]]/settings/` | `base.py`, `local.py`, `production.py`, `test.py` |
[[- end]]
[[- if .AppName]]
| `[[.AppName]]/models.py` | the model, its queryset and its database constraints |
| `[[.AppName]]/fields.py` | the ISBN field and the rules every write path (forms, admin, API) shares |
[[- if .REST]]
| `[[.AppName]]/api/` | [[if .Ninja]]the Ninja API, its router and schemas[[else]]serializers, viewsets and API URLs[[end]] |
[[- end]]
| `[[.AppName]]/templates/` | the pages for this app |
[[- end]]
| `templates/` | base layout, home page and error pages |
| `static/` | CSS and JavaScript |
[[- if .Tailwind]]
| `assets/tailwind.css` | Tailwind input; compiled to `static/dist/styles.css`, kept out of `static/` so `collectstatic` never sees it |
[[- end]]

